      errorSystemMessage: 
      userPrompt: 
      TicketPrompt: 'Fix the success-driven sunrise lighting in the active word-choice
        scene. The directional-light rotations currently move the apparent sun downward:
        adjust the pre-dawn and morning rotations, preserving the existing horizontal
        direction, so the warm sun starts below the horizon and outside the camera
        view, then rises clearly above the horizon as correct choices accumulate.
        Retain the existing intensity, ambient, and sky-color interpolation tied
        to correct answers.'
      ChatResponses:
        Answers:
        - Content: "Corrected the sunrise rotation behavior in the active word-choice
            scene. The sun now began below the horizon and rose clearly into view
            as correct answers accumulated, while preserving its existing horizontal
            direction.\n\n## Changes made\n\n- **Rotation endpoints:** Updated the
            pre-dawn and morning rotations on the scene\u2019s sunrise controller,
            retaining the `-30\xB0` yaw and correcting only the vertical movement.\n-
            **Lighting progression:** Preserved the existing success-count progression,
            intensity and light-color interpolation, ambient trilight blending, and
            camera sky-color transitions.\n- **Scene configuration:** Applied the
            corrected serialized rotation values to the active `GameManager`, keeping
            the initial state dark with the sun outside the camera view."
          SecondsSincePrevious: 16
          GeneratedAtTicks: 639241415677438120
          ResponseType: 3
